{
  "name": "l0_sprite_lifecycle",
  "about": "`CSprite`'s server lifecycle (a `fire` input is queued and delivered on the next fixed step, 1/60 s after its `t`; an `entity_call Use` runs at its `t`) (`walks/L0-r013.md`) over six `env_sprite`s created at runtime (a map row's Spawn runs the same bodies at Load). `CSprite::Spawn` 0x1042e550: `SetSolid(0)`, `SetMoveType(0, 0)`, `m_flFrame = 0`, `Precache` 0x1042e8c0 (no aim entity: `m_hAttachedToEntity` -1, `m_nAttachment` 0), `CSprite::SetModel` 0x1042e850 (a non-sprite model only Msgs), `m_flMaxFrame = frames - 1` from the engine's model frame count (`VEngineServer014` slot 26; the `sprite_model` fixtures stand for its table: candle 8 frames, a 2-frame model, glowa 1), then `m_iName == 0 || spawnflags & 1` -> TurnOn else TurnOff, the angle arm (`yaw != 0 && roll == 0` -> `SetAngles(pitch, 0, yaw)`: the yaw moves into the roll slot), the scale clamp to [0, 8] with its DevMsg (0 passes through as 0), `m_nBrightness = renderamt`, `m_flSpriteScale = clamped`, the two times 0. TurnOn `FUN_1042ef70`: `m_fEffects &= ~0x40`; `(framerate != 0 && m_flMaxFrame > 1.0 (a DOUBLE)) || spawnflags & 2` installs `m_pfnThink` = 0x10011757 (AnimateThink) with `m_flNextThink = m_flLastTime = curtime`; `m_flFrame = 0` always -- so a 2-frame sprite never schedules and a once-sprite (flag 2) schedules with no frames at all. TurnOff `FUN_1042ef40`: `m_flNextThink = 0`, `m_fEffects |= 0x40`, the think word untouched. `CSprite::Use` 0x1042f030: `state = (m_fEffects != 0x40)` then `ShouldToggle` 0x100a98f0 (OFF on an off sprite is refused; ON turns it on; TOGGLE flips); the inputs `HideSprite` 0x1042f080 / `ShowSprite` 0x1042f0a0 / `TurnOn` 0x1042f110 / `TurnOff` 0x1042f130 are TurnOff / TurnOn, and `ToggleSprite` 0x1042f0c0 compares the WHOLE word with 0x40, so an authored `effects 96` (NODRAW|NOSHADOW) always takes TurnOff and never shows. AnimateThink `FUN_1042eca0` adds `(curtime - last) * framerate` through AnimateFrame `FUN_1042ee50` (past the maximum: flag 2 TurnOffs without wrapping, else `fmod` when `m_flMaxFrame > 0`) and then re-arms `m_flNextThink = curtime`, so a finished once-sprite keeps thinking while hidden. Reported as `fail`, a stored word, a schedule or a site payload differs from retail's.",
  "stage": "arena",
  "seed": 1,
  "duration": 1.6,
